# Hydrate quality lock (do not regress)

These were already fixed once and leaked back after unrelated hydrate/KC work. **Do not** remove or bypass the post-process. `npm test` must stay green.

## Invariants (code, not prompts)

- **Cover title:** at most 8 words. `shortenCourseTitle` after file analysis and outline.
- **Module title:** short topic label, no Bloom gerunds. `shortenModuleTitle` after outline coverage.
- **Markdown glyphs:** `**bold**` and `###` never show as raw symbols. Choice-card body/reveal/prompt go through `markdownToHtml`. Quiz options and other plain-text surfaces use `stripMarkdownArtifacts`.
- **One instruction** on choice-cards: `collapseChoiceCardsOst`. Click-reveal intro that is only a “Select each…” line is dropped; the player shows Overview + CTA on the left and shorter reveal rows on the right (`ClickRevealInteraction`).
- **Image prompts:** `buildGroundedVisualPrompt` — never label-only; no typeset text in the photo (`imageVisualPrompt.test.ts`).
- **Key takeaways** are learner statements (`normalizeKeyTakeaways`), not spec-table rows or empty numbered cards.
- **Knowledge checks** always have a learner payload and **empty** `voiceOverText` (`ensureKnowledgeCheckPayload` + `stripSlideNarration`). Never convert an incomplete quiz to a `content` slide titled “Knowledge Check”.
- **KC count/place:** `ensureKnowledgeCheckBudget` + `alignHydratedSlidesToOutline`. Teaching slides cannot become quizzes.
- **Enabling coverage:** one module per terminal, 1–2 teaching slides per enabling (`ensureEnablingSlideCoverage`).
- **Teaching slides** are not a single thin subtitle (`teachingSlideNeedsRetry` + `finalizeHydratedSlide`).
- **Tab intro** never includes “Select a tab…” (`formatTabIntroOst`).
- **Review script** matches player order/OST (`reviewAlignment.test.ts`).

## How to change generation

Put new hydrate/QC/review behavior **behind these helpers**, then add a failing test first. Prompt-only rules will drift; the lock is the post-process plus `npm test`.
